# Logos ABI-closure exemptions — read by `logosc --abi-closure --abi-exempt`.
#
# The spec must be CLOSED: every type named by a recorded field list or enum
# payload must itself have a record. A line here says "this one does not, and
# here is the reason the EMITTER computes for it". Format:
#
#   <fully.qualified.Type>\t<reason>          (TAB-separated; # = comment)
#
# ⚠ AN EXEMPTION CANNOT OUTLIVE ITS CAUSE, AND THAT IS MECHANIZED, NOT PROMISED.
#   • the reason is not asserted here, it is COMPARED against what the emitter
#     derives this build. If the cause changes — the type becomes `pub`, or the
#     deem policy stops dropping it — the reasons disagree and the gate FAILS
#     with EXEMPTION-REASON-CHANGED. Rewriting the reason here to match is a
#     deliberate act, not a silent drift.
#   • an exemption that matches no violation FAILS with EXEMPTION-STALE. That is
#     also the canary for the whole check: if the closure walk ever stops
#     reaching (the one way this gate could report "closed" while seeing
#     nothing), every exemption below goes unmatched and the run goes RED
#     instead of green. A dead check cannot pass here.
#
# REASONS THE EMITTER CAN DERIVE:
#   not-pub                        private type reached BY VALUE from a record.
#                                  NOT exemptible: it fixes the public record's
#                                  size, so a consumer that stack-allocates the
#                                  public type is built against it.
#   not-pub-behind-indirection     private type reached only through a pointer.
#   deem-outside-derived-api-closure   in a deem package and not reachable from
#                                  the dynamic-query API seed.
#   wql-internal-pkg / canon-internal-pkg   engine-internal package.
#   unknown-origin                 no declaration seen in any compiled layer.
#
# ── the population, as of this commit ────────────────────────────────────────
# Both entries are the SAME shape and neither has anything to do with the deem
# policy that motivated this check: a module-private struct reached only through
# a `*mut` field of a public one. Nothing outside its own module can name the
# type, so no consumer can be compiled against its shape; and because every edge
# to it is indirect, the public record's own size does not depend on it. If
# either becomes `pub`, or is ever embedded by value, the reason the emitter
# derives changes and this file stops matching.
#
# `HashMap.entries: *mut Entry<K, V>` (+ HashMapIter/Keys/Values)
logos.mem.collections.hashmap.Entry	not-pub-behind-indirection
# `Bytes.inner: *mut BytesInner` (+ BytesMut)
logos.std.io.bytes.BytesInner	not-pub-behind-indirection
